I've been reading the Beginners guide off and on to learn the
grammer/syntax, although I've never actually done the exercises in
writting before. I'll have to try taking to time to translate/read
some things in the near future, even though I was wanting to learn
some more basic vocab before I tried anything like that.

And thanks for the link to the pdf dictionary, it is in a fairly
easier to use format then the jbovlaste site for basic usage.

On Sat, Jan 17, 2009 at 5:09 PM, Yoav Nir <yoav.nir@gmail.com> wrote:
> This is just my opinion:
>
> Get a dictionary. Either create it on jbovlaste, or else download from
> http://public.me.com/yoavetali (get ld.pdf) It's a little nicer formatted,
> and I update it every month.
> Read through "Lojban for Beginners", and actually do the exercises in
> writing.
> After that, try to translate some stuff. Start with simple things, like Dr.
> Seuss or songs (don't worry about rhymes). You'll always have to look things
> up, and that's how you learn.
> Reading also helps, and there's some translated stuff on the lojban.org
> website. It is tiresome at first when you have to look up every other word.
>
